    "sloc": 79,
    "title": "Plain Bitonic Sort",
    "description": "Pad to a power of two with +inf, then for every stage k and distance j put each pair (i, i+j) in order -- ascending where bit k of i is clear. Distances below one 2048-key tile run in shared memory, larger ones as global passes. Runs unchanged on the BMG and the H100.",
    "idioms": [
      "def-grid-function merge-in-tile: a barrier-holding helper (dec-times-by-half+ over the distances)",
      "do-power-step+ over the stages inside one tile",
      "grid-stride over the pairs of one global distance",
      "(declare (uniform from)): a parameter as a provably uniform loop bound"
    ],
